+The scheduler writes at the pid, as bookkeeping and as the process:
+\begin{itemize}
+\item a snapshot, when a setup or a compute returns a value not equal to the
+  one it last wrote there;
+\item an empty list of patches, when a run ends with a status other than the
+  one last written.
+\end{itemize}
+A run that ends with an error equal to the last changes nothing, so a
+process that keeps failing the same way stops. The scheduler writes pending
+before a run ends only where a read could otherwise take an out-of-date
+value as current. When a read through an interface it bound reaches a due
+process's node, and is not stopped (Order), the scheduler first writes that
+process's pending, so the read shows it. When a request ends, it writes
+pending for each process still due.
 
